---
description: Recording Studio data and API conventions for gems and host apps
alwaysApply: true
---

Prefer Recording Studio public helpers over private registrar internals.

Recordables are immutable snapshots. Use `revise` to change state and `log_event!` for history. Do not write `Event` rows directly.

Declare every configured recordable with `recording_studio_recordable`, including `root` and `allowed_parent_types`. Validate declarations in tests.

Roots are the content and billing buckets. Users and other actors get access to roots; they do not own the tree. Prefer actors over user-only designs, and use Recording Studio Accessible for access.

Keep addon gems focused and reusable across apps. Prefer extracting shared behavior into `recording-studio-*` gems over one-off app code. Capability mixins are opt-in and do not come for free from type registration.

Get Recording Studio working with defaults first; host apps configure settings and override views when needed. Keep screens simple and one primary action per page, using Flatpack and the core default layout.

Preserve public APIs unless the user asks for a breaking change. Use Conventional Commits when a version bump is required.
